WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.034 --> 00:00:01.468
The US

00:00:01.468 --> 00:00:02.302
Treasury Department

00:00:02.302 --> 00:00:02.902
is expected

00:00:02.902 --> 00:00:03.703
to designate

00:00:03.703 --> 00:00:05.338
the Russian mercenary organization,

00:00:05.338 --> 00:00:06.506
the Bognor Group,

00:00:06.506 --> 00:00:08.842
as a transnational criminal organization

00:00:08.842 --> 00:00:09.642
with links to North

00:00:09.642 --> 00:00:11.011
Korea Russian President

00:00:11.011 --> 00:00:11.644
Vladimir Putin

00:00:11.644 --> 00:00:13.480
has increasingly relied on Wagner

00:00:13.480 --> 00:00:17.017
to carry out operations in Ukraine

00:00:17.350 --> 00:00:18.485
As we have said publicly.

00:00:18.485 --> 00:00:19.519
North Korea delivered

00:00:19.519 --> 00:00:21.921
infantry rockets and missiles into Russia

00:00:22.022 --> 00:00:23.890
for use by Wagner

00:00:23.890 --> 00:00:25.959
toward the end of last year.

00:00:25.959 --> 00:00:27.694
Bodner is a criminal organization

00:00:27.694 --> 00:00:29.496
that is continuing wide

00:00:29.496 --> 00:00:29.796
sorry,

00:00:29.796 --> 00:00:30.864
committing widespread

00:00:30.864 --> 00:00:34.067
atrocities and human rights abuses.

00:00:34.067 --> 00:00:35.301
CNN's Oren Liebermann

00:00:35.301 --> 00:00:37.203
joins us from the Pentagon now or

00:00:37.203 --> 00:00:39.472
and what does this new designation mean?

00:00:40.707 --> 00:00:42.242
First, it means that Wagner

00:00:42.242 --> 00:00:44.010
and those entities associated with it,

00:00:44.010 --> 00:00:45.145
perhaps not only in Ukraine,

00:00:45.145 --> 00:00:46.046
but other places

00:00:46.046 --> 00:00:47.981
Wagner operates, such as Africa.

00:00:47.981 --> 00:00:49.816
Syria will face more sanctions

00:00:49.816 --> 00:00:50.784
from the US government.

00:00:50.784 --> 00:00:52.285
It's also a strong statement

00:00:52.285 --> 00:00:54.054
about how the US views Wagner,

00:00:54.054 --> 00:00:56.056
a mercenary group used by Russia,

00:00:56.256 --> 00:00:57.891
as an additional force.

00:00:57.891 --> 00:01:00.293
The US recently declassified photos,

00:01:00.293 --> 00:01:02.429
it says, are of a Russian train

00:01:02.429 --> 00:01:03.930
crossing into North Korea.

00:01:03.930 --> 00:01:06.099
About five cars on that Russian train

00:01:06.099 --> 00:01:07.067
picking up ammo.

00:01:07.067 --> 00:01:08.501
You can see the images there

00:01:08.501 --> 00:01:09.969
taking that ammo from North Korea

00:01:09.969 --> 00:01:10.937
and bringing it back

00:01:10.937 --> 00:01:12.138
to the fight in Ukraine.

00:01:12.138 --> 00:01:12.806
That's the part of this

00:01:12.806 --> 00:01:13.773
that makes for ordinary

00:01:13.773 --> 00:01:15.842
transnational criminal organization

00:01:16.142 --> 00:01:16.576
The U.S.

00:01:16.576 --> 00:01:17.577
had talked about this

00:01:17.577 --> 00:01:18.645
just a couple of weeks ago,

00:01:18.645 --> 00:01:19.979
but late last year.

00:01:19.979 --> 00:01:21.047
And here, they say,

00:01:21.047 --> 00:01:22.615
is the evidence, the photographs

00:01:22.615 --> 00:01:23.917
that back that up.

00:01:23.917 --> 00:01:25.718
Interestingly, it was Wagner

00:01:25.718 --> 00:01:26.986
that was using the artillery

00:01:26.986 --> 00:01:28.321
and the ammo provided here,

00:01:28.321 --> 00:01:30.590
not the Russian Ministry of Defense.

00:01:31.024 --> 00:01:32.192
And that gets out of how

00:01:32.192 --> 00:01:33.059
Wagner is operating,

00:01:33.059 --> 00:01:33.726
essentially

00:01:33.726 --> 00:01:34.961
a mercenary organization

00:01:34.961 --> 00:01:36.896
that is competing with at times

00:01:36.896 --> 00:01:37.564
and operating

00:01:37.564 --> 00:01:38.865
independently of

00:01:38.865 --> 00:01:40.467
the Russian military, primarily

00:01:40.467 --> 00:01:42.569
in Bermuda, a town in eastern Ukraine.

00:01:42.769 --> 00:01:44.637
That's where we've seen Wagner operating.

00:01:44.637 --> 00:01:45.505
According to the US,

00:01:45.505 --> 00:01:46.206
with a very

00:01:46.206 --> 00:01:48.208
high percentage of convicts,

00:01:48.208 --> 00:01:50.310
also filling in the shortages of,

00:01:50.310 --> 00:01:52.745
frankly, bodies in the Russian military

00:01:52.745 --> 00:01:54.013
that Russia is looking for

00:01:54.013 --> 00:01:56.382
and suffering heavy casualties as well.

00:01:56.549 --> 00:01:58.318
This is another step against Wagner

00:01:58.318 --> 00:01:59.752
coming from the U.S..

00:01:59.752 --> 00:02:01.354
Nic Robertson is CNN's international

00:02:01.354 --> 00:02:02.255
diplomatic editor.

00:02:02.255 --> 00:02:03.923
Jill Dougherty is a CNN contributor

00:02:03.923 --> 00:02:05.792
and former CNN Moscow bureau chief.

00:02:05.792 --> 00:02:07.494
Nic, what's the significance?

00:02:07.494 --> 00:02:08.461
What will change

00:02:08.461 --> 00:02:10.230
now that Bognor is designated

00:02:10.230 --> 00:02:12.332
as a criminal organization?

00:02:12.332 --> 00:02:13.633
It's going to make it harder for them

00:02:13.633 --> 00:02:15.335
to do business around the world.

00:02:15.335 --> 00:02:17.670
They've become an effective extension

00:02:17.670 --> 00:02:18.671
of the Russian state

00:02:18.671 --> 00:02:21.307
in some ways, extending their influence

00:02:21.841 --> 00:02:24.310
and moneymaking abilities from

00:02:24.310 --> 00:02:27.213
from Africa to the Middle East in Syria.

00:02:27.814 --> 00:02:29.949
And they've become a very effective

00:02:30.183 --> 00:02:31.451
fighting force in Ukraine.

00:02:31.451 --> 00:02:33.119
So blunting them

00:02:33.119 --> 00:02:34.354
is to

00:02:34.354 --> 00:02:35.622
blunting their abilities

00:02:35.622 --> 00:02:37.290
and trying to cut off money to them

00:02:37.290 --> 00:02:39.325
is to blunt their effectiveness

00:02:39.325 --> 00:02:41.194
and they're effective for Putin.

00:02:42.462 --> 00:02:44.130
Jill, we heard from

00:02:44.130 --> 00:02:45.131
John Kirby today

00:02:45.131 --> 00:02:47.100
that there is some concern

00:02:47.100 --> 00:02:48.268
within the Russian government

00:02:48.268 --> 00:02:51.104
about the recruiting practices

00:02:51.104 --> 00:02:51.971
of the Wagner group.

00:02:51.971 --> 00:02:53.473
80% of their mercenaries

00:02:53.473 --> 00:02:55.375
or fighters are convicts.

00:02:55.375 --> 00:02:57.510
There's also some disagreement

00:02:57.510 --> 00:02:58.444
over taking credit

00:02:58.444 --> 00:02:59.612
for the fight in Salvador.

00:02:59.612 --> 00:03:02.048
How fraught is the relationship

00:03:02.048 --> 00:03:04.284
between the Wagner group and promotion

00:03:04.284 --> 00:03:06.152
and the Russian government,

00:03:06.152 --> 00:03:07.787
military and Putin?

00:03:08.488 --> 00:03:10.590
You know, there's definitely tension

00:03:10.590 --> 00:03:14.394
between them because as you the Wagner

00:03:14.394 --> 00:03:16.596
group, used to be kind of in the shadows

00:03:17.463 --> 00:03:19.732
before all of this came out.

00:03:20.033 --> 00:03:22.202
And so now they're very much public

00:03:22.202 --> 00:03:24.270
and they have been claiming

00:03:24.270 --> 00:03:25.805
that they were the people

00:03:25.805 --> 00:03:27.473
who went into Solider

00:03:27.473 --> 00:03:29.943
and defeated the Ukrainians, etc.,

00:03:30.210 --> 00:03:31.678
and criticizing

00:03:31.678 --> 00:03:33.580
the regular Russian military

00:03:33.580 --> 00:03:35.215
for not being able to do that,

00:03:35.215 --> 00:03:37.650
for essentially screwing up the war.

00:03:37.951 --> 00:03:40.119
So this is really,

00:03:40.119 --> 00:03:43.623
I think, a significant back and forth

00:03:43.623 --> 00:03:45.225
between those two groups.

00:03:45.225 --> 00:03:46.059
It looks as if

00:03:46.059 --> 00:03:48.394
now you've got the government,

00:03:48.494 --> 00:03:50.029
Putin's government coming out

00:03:50.029 --> 00:03:52.298
war on the side of the regular military.

00:03:52.298 --> 00:03:54.334
But Wagner is really important.

00:03:54.334 --> 00:03:55.201
It is estimated

00:03:55.201 --> 00:03:55.768
that they have

00:03:55.768 --> 00:03:59.472
50,000 fighters in Ukraine right now.

00:03:59.672 --> 00:04:02.575
10,000 are contractors

00:04:02.775 --> 00:04:05.278
and the other 40 are prisoners

00:04:05.278 --> 00:04:07.447
who are let out in order to fight.

00:04:07.714 --> 00:04:08.915
And they have money.

00:04:08.915 --> 00:04:11.551
They're backed by oligarchs there.

00:04:11.551 --> 00:04:13.686
They're an important part

00:04:13.920 --> 00:04:14.387
of what

00:04:14.387 --> 00:04:16.256
Russia is trying to do in Ukraine,

00:04:16.256 --> 00:04:18.057
unfortunately. Hmm.

00:04:18.057 --> 00:04:21.728
Nick, we've learned that CIA chief U.S.

00:04:21.728 --> 00:04:22.662
intel

00:04:22.662 --> 00:04:24.430
officials are briefing

00:04:24.430 --> 00:04:26.299
or have briefed President Zelensky

00:04:26.299 --> 00:04:29.168
about this coming Russian offensive.

00:04:30.069 --> 00:04:31.404
What do we know

00:04:31.404 --> 00:04:32.639
about what that would look like?

00:04:33.673 --> 00:04:35.308
The potential is for Russia

00:04:35.308 --> 00:04:36.776
to have reequiped

00:04:36.776 --> 00:04:39.812
and retrained a large number of troops.

00:04:39.812 --> 00:04:41.247
We know that they said

00:04:41.247 --> 00:04:42.015
that they recruited

00:04:42.015 --> 00:04:43.883
about 300,000 forces

00:04:43.883 --> 00:04:45.218
towards the end of last year.

00:04:45.218 --> 00:04:45.818
It's believed

00:04:45.818 --> 00:04:46.386
they committed

00:04:46.386 --> 00:04:47.987
about 100,000 of those

00:04:47.987 --> 00:04:49.756
to the fight in Ukraine already.

00:04:49.756 --> 00:04:50.657
There's potential

00:04:50.657 --> 00:04:51.758
only an estimated

00:04:51.758 --> 00:04:55.528
a hundred to 150,000 of them left

00:04:55.828 --> 00:04:56.262
who could

00:04:56.262 --> 00:04:58.831
well have been given the training,

00:04:58.831 --> 00:05:00.233
the all those others that have been used

00:05:00.233 --> 00:05:02.035
as cannon fodder on the front lines

00:05:02.035 --> 00:05:03.169
haven't been given.

00:05:03.169 --> 00:05:03.870
Just this week,

00:05:03.870 --> 00:05:04.737
President Putin

00:05:04.737 --> 00:05:06.873
visited an armaments factory.

00:05:06.873 --> 00:05:08.975
He commended them for that.

00:05:08.975 --> 00:05:11.277
Their work told them how important it was

00:05:11.611 --> 00:05:12.945
mentioned that they were working

00:05:12.945 --> 00:05:16.849
20 473 shifts a day

00:05:17.016 --> 00:05:19.252
to keep production of armaments high

00:05:19.252 --> 00:05:21.020
because that's what's required.

00:05:21.020 --> 00:05:23.956
So, you know, it seems at the moment that

00:05:25.224 --> 00:05:26.693
Russia is getting itself

00:05:26.693 --> 00:05:28.795
ready to launch another offensive.

00:05:28.795 --> 00:05:30.463
And the clock is ticking on that.

00:05:30.463 --> 00:05:32.131
And that's made the conversations

00:05:32.131 --> 00:05:32.899
in Germany

00:05:32.899 --> 00:05:34.967
about the possibility of sending tanks

00:05:34.967 --> 00:05:36.169
to Ukraine.

00:05:36.169 --> 00:05:37.470
All the more pressing

00:05:37.470 --> 00:05:39.172
Ukraine is listening

00:05:39.172 --> 00:05:40.707
to that sort of intelligence.

00:05:40.707 --> 00:05:41.974
And unlike the time

00:05:41.974 --> 00:05:43.643
before the war, a year ago,

00:05:43.643 --> 00:05:44.444
when they said

00:05:44.444 --> 00:05:45.378
they didn't believe

00:05:45.378 --> 00:05:46.646
an offensive was coming,

00:05:46.646 --> 00:05:48.281
this is much more critical.

00:05:48.281 --> 00:05:51.250
Russia if it comes back with a big push,

00:05:51.250 --> 00:05:51.918
with better

00:05:51.918 --> 00:05:54.020
trained, better equipped forces,

00:05:54.020 --> 00:05:55.922
better organized than previously.

00:05:55.922 --> 00:05:59.225
This is this is a potential worrying and

00:05:59.492 --> 00:06:01.494
and dangerous threat for Ukraine

00:06:01.494 --> 00:06:03.930
right now on the front lines in the east.

00:06:03.930 --> 00:06:05.565
Jill, is it likely.

00:06:05.565 --> 00:06:06.733
Are there signs that

00:06:06.733 --> 00:06:07.400
that Russia

00:06:07.400 --> 00:06:08.668
will be able to come

00:06:08.668 --> 00:06:09.502
with that better

00:06:09.502 --> 00:06:11.671
trained, better equipped,

00:06:11.671 --> 00:06:14.240
better strategized, better led

00:06:14.574 --> 00:06:15.875
fighting force in the spring?

00:06:17.477 --> 00:06:18.978
They may have learned

00:06:18.978 --> 00:06:20.012
something, you know,

00:06:20.012 --> 00:06:21.080
from bringing

00:06:21.080 --> 00:06:23.549
in during the last mobilization

00:06:23.750 --> 00:06:25.151
that started in September

00:06:25.151 --> 00:06:26.986
when you had a lot of regular

00:06:26.986 --> 00:06:28.888
guys from big cities

00:06:28.888 --> 00:06:30.923
being pulled into the military.

00:06:31.190 --> 00:06:31.891
They were

00:06:31.891 --> 00:06:33.493
there were multiple reports

00:06:33.493 --> 00:06:34.727
and we've talked about this

00:06:34.727 --> 00:06:35.895
where they went into the field

00:06:35.895 --> 00:06:37.930
with very limited kit,

00:06:37.930 --> 00:06:39.766
you know, not enough weapons,

00:06:39.766 --> 00:06:40.933
not enough supplies.

00:06:40.933 --> 00:06:43.002
Their families were providing

00:06:43.002 --> 00:06:44.604
some of what they needed.

00:06:44.604 --> 00:06:45.538
But so far,

00:06:45.538 --> 00:06:46.606
it appears that

00:06:46.606 --> 00:06:50.143
the Kremlin has improved on that.

00:06:50.343 --> 00:06:51.944
But it's still there

00:06:51.944 --> 00:06:53.946
the way they command their troops.

00:06:53.946 --> 00:06:55.114
And the preparation

00:06:55.114 --> 00:06:56.516
is not

00:06:56.649 --> 00:06:59.152
at all on the level of what Neato does.

00:06:59.419 --> 00:07:02.522
So it's it's a matter of personnel

00:07:02.855 --> 00:07:06.626
and weapons and strategy

00:07:06.793 --> 00:07:09.395
And that's where the Russians often fail.

